# Compliance artifacts must be localized (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-08-16): **localize rules for products.**
The following compliance surfaces are **must-localize** — English-only
shipping text is a defect.

## The rule

> **Every compliance artifact this product shows, exports, or files must
> have localized catalogs for every shipped content language (`en`, `de`,
> `fr`, `es` today). Preferred language on the person record wins when
> set; otherwise the page cookie / Accept-Language / English. Operators
> can edit each language’s version. Official regulation text stays in
> the language the authority published; AIC chrome, mappings, notices,
> and summaries are localized.**

## Must-localize list

| Artifact | Typical home |
| --- | --- |
| Audit reports | Report Center catalogs + export chrome |
| Evidence exports | Binder / auditor package export |
| Policy documentation | Playbooks, policy templates, docs |
| Risk assessment templates | Risks catalogs + SPA `risks` |
| Regulatory mappings (IEC 62443, NERC CIP, CMMC, ISO 27001) | Catalog + binder mapping chrome |
| Legal text (privacy, data handling, retention, chain-of-custody) | Disclosures + legal notices |
| Session recording evidence summaries | Recording / session evidence chrome |
| Access control evidence | IAM / access evidence reports |
| Change management logs | Change / CM evidence views |
| Incident response documentation | IR playbooks, notices, exports |
| Data processing agreements | Legal / DPA templates |
| Consent and privacy notices | Disclosures, welcome, training |
| Compliance dashboards | Dashboard / CSC / operations chrome |

A new row on this list lands with EN + DE + FR + ES catalog keys in the
same change set (or an honest **BLOCKED** with the missing tag named).

## How locale is chosen

1. Person **preferred language** (`ui_locale`) when set.
2. Else web cookie / language selector / `Accept-Language`.
3. Else English.

Empty preferred language is **Not Set**, not English-forced.

## Official text vs AIC prose

| Kind | Localize? |
| --- | --- |
| AIC labels, dashboard chrome, export headings, notices, DPA/consent we author | **Yes** — all shipped tags |
| AIC mapping explanations and crosswalk summaries | **Yes** |
| Official CMMC / NIST 800-53 / 800-171 control bodies | Keep the authority language (English) |
| ISO 27001 licensed control text | Do **not** translate or paste — identifiers + AIC summary only |
| GDPR / NIS2 official translations | Use the published language text, cited |

Localizing a mapping is not a **Met** or certified claim
([`compliance-claims-honesty.mdc`](compliance-claims-honesty.mdc)).

## Required agent behavior

1. New or edited text on a must-localize surface goes through catalogs
   (`locales/<tag>/`, SPA `ui/src/i18n/locales/<tag>/`, or
   `offline_localized_copy`) — not hardcoded English-only in TSX/Rust.
2. Administrators can edit each language (Defaults, templates, binder
   copy) without replacing the English inheritance row.
3. Exports and Email/SMS use the recipient’s preferred language when set.
4. Mirror this rule to `core-assets/.cursor/rules/` in the same change
   set ([`auto-commit-push.mdc`](auto-commit-push.mdc)).

## Forbidden

- Shipping any row in the must-localize list in English only when other
  content languages already ship.
- Translating copyrighted ISO control text, or inventing unofficial
  CMMC / 800-53 body translations and calling them the control.
- Claiming a dashboard, binder export, or report is localized because
  the nav label translated.
- Writing preferred language from the page cookie onto the profile.

